# deploy/systemd/DIVERGENCES — reference-copy vs .j2-template directive
# disagreements that predate lint-deploy-systemd-authority.sh's content
# check (RLT-434, issue #818) and are not yet reconciled.
#
# The reference copy under deploy/systemd/ is documentation; the .j2 in
# the role is what's actually deployed. Declaring an entry here says
# "this pre-existing gap is known and tracked", not "this is correct" —
# nobody has confirmed which side matches production, and closing an
# entry means making the two agree (usually: updating the reference copy
# to match what actually runs), then deleting the line.
# scripts/ci/lint-deploy-systemd-authority.sh fails on any UNDECLARED
# divergence between a reference copy and its template twin.
#
# Format: <unit>:<directive>  # why it's still open

# The deployed template wraps the binary in run-heavy-job.sh (lock +
# ops_batch identity logging, 14-stellarindex-services.yml); these
# reference copies predate that wrapper and still show a bare ExecStart.
archive-completeness.service:ExecStart
galexie-archive-trim.service:ExecStart
verify-archive-tier-a.service:ExecStart
verify-archive-tier-b.service:ExecStart

# Reference and template disagree on which env file the unit reads.
# Which one matches what's actually on r1 has not been confirmed.
stellarindex-aggregator.service:EnvironmentFile
stellarindex-api.service:EnvironmentFile
stellarindex-indexer.service:EnvironmentFile
supply-snapshot.service:EnvironmentFile

# Cosmetic wording drift in the [Unit] Description= line; harmless but
# undeclared.
stellarindex-aggregator.service:Description
stellarindex-api.service:Description
stellarindex-indexer.service:Description

# The template queues on run-heavy-job.sh's shared tier-A/B lock
# (HEAVY_JOB_LOCK_WAIT=72000), so READY=1 can come up to 20h after start;
# the wrapper-less reference copies keep the bare 10m start budget.
verify-archive-tier-a.service:TimeoutStartSec
verify-archive-tier-b.service:TimeoutStartSec

# The templates queue on run-heavy-job.sh's host-wide and scheduled locks
# (HEAVY_JOB_LOCK_WAIT=43200), so TimeoutStartSec covers a 12h wait plus the
# run; the wrapper-less reference copies keep the bare run-only budget.
archive-completeness.service:TimeoutStartSec
galexie-archive-trim.service:TimeoutStartSec
